    .{ .slug = "multicolumn", .title = "CSS3 Multiple column layout", .search = "CSS3 Multiple column layout multicolumn column-count,column-width,column-gap,column-rule,column-rule-type,column-span,column-fill,break-before,break-after,break-inside", .description = "Method of flowing information in multiple columns", .notes = "", .summary = .{ "154 Partial (#3)", "156 Partial (#4)", "27 Full", "152 Partial (#3)" }, .details = .{ "Version history: 4–49: Partial (prefix required, #1, #2); 50–154: Partial (#3).\n#1: Does not support the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside. WebKit- and Blink-based browsers have equivalent support with the non-standard -webkit-column-break-* properties, but only for the values auto and always. Firefox does not support the break-* properties but supports the now-obsolete page-break-* properties in the paging (printing) context.\n#2: Does not support the column-fill property.\n#3: Does not support the values avoid (in the column context), avoid-column, and avoid-page for the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside; does not support the value column for the properties break-after and break-before.", "Version history: 2–51: Partial (prefix required, #1); 52–64: Partial (#1); 65–91: Partial (#3); 92–156: Partial (#4).\n#1: Does not support the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside. WebKit- and Blink-based browsers have equivalent support with the non-standard -webkit-column-break-* properties, but only for the values auto and always. Firefox does not support the break-* properties but supports the now-obsolete page-break-* properties in the paging (printing) context.\n#3: Does not support the values avoid (in the column context), avoid-column, and avoid-page for the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside; does not support the value column for the properties break-after and break-before.\n#4: Does not support the values avoid (in the column context) for the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside; does not support the values avoid-column, avoid-page, and column for the properties break-before and break-after.", "Version history: 3.1–6.1: Partial (prefix required, #1, #2); 7–8: Partial (prefix required, #1); 9–9.1: Partial (#1); 10–27: Full.\n#1: Does not support the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside. WebKit- and Blink-based browsers have equivalent support with the non-standard -webkit-column-break-* properties, but only for the values auto and always. Firefox does not support the break-* properties but supports the now-obsolete page-break-* properties in the paging (printing) context.\n#2: Does not support the column-fill property.", "Version history: 12–18: Full; 79–152: Partial (#3).\n#3: Does not support the values avoid (in the column context), avoid-column, and avoid-page for the properties break-after, break-before, and break-inside; does not support the value column for the properties break-after and break-before." } },
