    .{ .slug = "intrinsic-width", .title = "Intrinsic & Extrinsic Sizing", .search = "Intrinsic & Extrinsic Sizing intrinsic-width fill,fill-available,max-content,min-content,fit-content,contain-floats,intrinsic,extrinsic,sizing", .description = "Allows for the heights and widths to be specified in intrinsic values using the max-content, min-content, fit-content and stretch (formerly fill) properties.", .notes = "Prefixes are on the values, not the property names (e.g. -webkit-min-content) Older webkit browsers also support the unofficial intrinsic value which acts the same as max-content.", .summary = .{ "154 Full (#4)", "156 Partial (#2, #5)", "27 Full", "152 Full (#4)" }, .details = .{ "Version history: 4–21: No; 22–45: Full (prefix required, #3); 46–93: Full (#3, #4); 94–154: Full (#4).\n#3: Does not support the flex-basis property. See specs, Blink bug, Firefox bug.\n#4: Chrome does not yet unprefix stretch (aka fill/fill-available), because the CSSWG is not ready for that yet. See Chromium bug.", "Version history: 2: No; 3–65: Partial (prefix required, #1, #2, #3); 66–156: Partial (#2, #5).\n#1: Firefox does not support the height/min-height/max-height properties, only width. See test case, Firefox bug.\n#2: Firefox supports the -moz-available keyword rather than stretch. Firefox bug.\n#3: Does not support the flex-basis property. See specs, Blink bug, Firefox bug.\n#5: While still being affected by note 1, it is only for -moz-fit-content and -moz-available.", "Version history: 3.1–6: No; 6.1–8: Partial (prefix required, #1, #3); 9–10.1: Partial (prefix required, #3); 11–15.6: Partial (#3); 16.0–27: Full.\n#1: Firefox does not support the height/min-height/max-height properties, only width. See test case, Firefox bug.\n#3: Does not support the flex-basis property. See specs, Blink bug, Firefox bug.", "Version history: 12–18: No; 79–93: Full (#3, #4); 94–152: Full (#4).\n#3: Does not support the flex-basis property. See specs, Blink bug, Firefox bug.\n#4: Chrom