    .{ .slug = "clipboard", .title = "Synchronous Clipboard API", .search = "Synchronous Clipboard API clipboard cut,copy,paste,clipboarddata,clipboardevent", .description = "API to provide copy, cut and paste events as well as provide access to the OS clipboard.", .notes = "Internet Explorer will display a security prompt for access to the OS clipboard. Chrome 42+, Opera 29+ and Firefox 41+ support clipboard reading/writing only when part of a user action (click, keydown, etc).", .summary = .{ "154 Partial (#7)", "156 Partial (#6)", "27 Full", "152 Partial (#7)" }, .details = .{ "Version history: 4–12: No; 13–42: Partial (#3, #5); 43–57: Partial (#5, #7); 58–154: Partial (#7).\n#3: Only supports OS clipboard reading/writing via shortcut keys, not through document.execCommand().\n#5: Does not support the ClipboardEvent constructor\n#7: Supports cut & copy events without a focused editable field, but does not fire paste with document.execCommand('paste')", "Version history: 2–21: No; 22–40: Partial (#2, #3); 41–156: Partial (#6).\n#2: Only fires copy event on a valid selection and only cut and paste in focused editable fields.\n#3: Only supports OS clipboard reading/writing via shortcut keys, not through document.execCommand().\n#6: Supports cut & copy events without a focused editable field, but not paste (presumably for security reasons)", "Version history: 3.1–3.2: Unknown; 4–9.1: Partial (#2, #3, #5); 10–11.1: Partial (#2, #5); 12–27: Full.\n#2: Only fires copy event on a valid selection and only cut and paste in focused editable fields.\n#3: Only supports OS clipboard reading/writing via shortcut keys, not through document.execCommand().\n#5: Does not support the ClipboardEvent constructor", "Version history: 12–16: Partial (#1, #2, #5); 17–18: Partial (#2); 79–152: Partial (#7).\n#1: Only supports Text and URL data types and uses a non-standard method of interacting with the clipboard.\n#2: Only fires copy event on a valid selection and only cut and paste in fo